TI  - Bempedoic Acid (ETC-1002): A Current Review
PY  - 2018
T2  - Cardiology Clinics
VL  - 36
IS  - 2
SP  - 257
EP  - 264
DO  - 10.1016/j.ccl.2017.12.007
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85042202082&doi=10.1016%2fj.ccl.2017.12.007&partnerID=40&md5=5e5b879d69b78dbbe9bec2215a4a2c69
AB  - Although statins are first-line therapy for low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) reduction, many individuals on maximally tolerated statin therapy have elevated LDL-C. Bempedoic acid (ETC-1002) is a novel once-daily LDL-C–lowering agent in phase 3 clinical trials. In phase 1 and 2 studies, ETC-1002 was efficacious in lowering LDL-C when used as monotherapy and when added to statin and/or ezetimibe and was well tolerated in patients with statin intolerance. ETC-1002 also improved cardiometabolic risk factors. Ongoing phase 3 studies of ETC-1002 are evaluating its long-term efficacy and safety, and effects on cardiovascular events. This article discusses current evidence and future directions for ETC-1002. © 2017 Elsevier Inc.
